  Cleaver is a two-handed weapon.  This can be fatal if cursed in
Gehennom.  It also means no shield.

  Barbarians can #twoweapon.  #twoweaponing with a secondary silver
saber is almost always better than any twohanded weapon, even artifacts,
because:
  - Can enchant both weapons.
  - Silver damage vs demons.
    - There are no silver two-handed weapons.
  - Strength damage bonus on both weapons.

  If your secondary weapon gets cursed it slips from your hands.
   - Can be embarrassing or worse if not noticed.
   - Can't get both hands welded to weapons if #twoweaponing
     - This would be just as bad as wielded a cursed two-handed weapon.

  On the Ascension Run, when you should be running, not fighting, you
can switch to singleweaponing and wearing a +7 elven shield: 9AC total.

>The Cleaver is neutral aligned. So is there a good reason to be chaotic 
>aligned instead of neutral, when playing as a barbarian?

  Cleaver will be adjusted to your starting alignment, whatever it is.
This has no effect on Cleaver.

  What your alignment will affect is:
   Chaotics:
    - don't get "You murderer!" and telepathy loss.
    - can same race sacrifice safely.
      - Same race sacrifice on any alter converts it to chaotic
        - guaranteed
    - Alignment boost for consorting with foocubi.
    - Possible divine gifts when #offering.
    - Can't purify/heal by quaffing holy water.


  Possible divine gifts might be important, if you have enough patience.
Magicbane and Mjollnir are Neutral.  Frost Brand is unaligned, so is
unaffected by the decision.

  Stormbringer is the crowning Chaotic gift.  Vorpal Blade is the
crowning Neutral gift.  

  Not much to choose between the two crowning gifts.  Vorpal Blade isn't
that great to begin with, but won't attack peacefuls.  Demons and undead
are drain resistant.  Stormbringer does provide level drain resistance.

  


